   "text": {
    "L1": "Work can be economic or non-economic. The key question is whether payment is involved.",
    "L2": "Economic activities earn money or payment in kind and produce goods or services.",
    "L3": "Non-economic activities are done without payment, out of love, care, duty, service or joy.",
    "L4": "Unpaid work at home is real work. Cooking, cleaning and caring help families function and must be respected.",
    "L5": "The same activity can be either kind of work, depending on its purpose and payment.",
    "L6": "Teaching in a school for a salary is economic. Helping your own child with homework is non-economic.",
    "L7": "All honest work has dignity, and people depend on each other's work every day."
   },
